cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material for teaching or research, please cite the lecture notes below."
title: "Quantitative Methods in Finance — companion code"
abstract: >-
  Executable companion to the lecture notes "Quantitative Methods in Finance" and the primer
  "Mathematics for Finance: A Self-Contained Primer" by Eric Vansteenberghe, taught in the
  Quantitative Methods in Finance and Financial Econometrics lectures at Université Paris 1
  Panthéon-Sorbonne. Python and R implementations of probability, simulation, regression,
  time-series, risk and insurance methods.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vansteenberghe
    given-names: Eric
    affiliation: "Banque de France; Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne"
repository-code: "https://github.com/skimeur/QMF"
url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.12896"
